  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "Find $y(t)$ given that the Laplace transform of the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2033}(t)+y(t)=7,\\,y(0)=7,\\,{y}^{\u2032}(0)=0\n$$\n\nis given by\n\n$$\n{s}^{2}Y(s)+Y(s)=\\frac{7(1+{s}^{2})}{s}.\n$$\n\nThe solution is $y(t)=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "Using the transformed equation, we can solve for $Y(s)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}^{2}Y(s)+Y(s) & =\\frac{7(1+{s}^{2})}{s} \\\\ ({s}^{2}+1)Y(s) & =\\frac{7(1+{s}^{2})}{s} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{7}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is valid for $s>0.$\n\nNow, taking the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}(Y(s)) & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{7}{s}} \\\\ y(t) & =7{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}} \\\\ y(t) & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
